Compare two versions of a package and report what changed

Scans both sides and reports findings that appeared, findings that were resolved, and structural changes (upstream, install scripts, functions) that a severity count alone would hide. Keeps no state, so it is safe in CI; `check` and `install` do this automatically against your scan history.

Usage: aur-scan diff [OPTIONS] <OLD> <NEW>

Arguments:
  <OLD>
          The older package directory (or PKGBUILD)

  <NEW>
          The newer package directory (or PKGBUILD)

Options:
  -f, --format <FORMAT>
          Output format
          
          [default: text]
          [possible values: text, json]

      --fail-on <FAIL_ON>
          Exit non-zero if a NEWLY ADDED finding is at or above this severity. Pre-existing findings never trip this gate
          
          [possible values: critical, high, medium, low, info]

  -c, --config <CONFIG>
          Configuration file path

  -s, --severity <SEVERITY>
          Minimum severity to report
          
          [possible values: critical, high, medium, low, info]

  -v, --verbose
          Enable verbose output

  -q, --quiet
          Quiet mode (only show findings)

      --no-color
          Disable colored output (also honored: the NO_COLOR environment variable)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
